+/*
+ * ConfigurationTab — landscape-phone layout for the config category picker.
+ * Issue #5069.
+ *
+ * WHAT WAS WRONG
+ * --------------
+ * The picker (`SectionNav`) is a sticky wrapping button grid. With 28
+ * categories it wrapped to five rows: measured at 844x390 it was 208px tall
+ * inside 302px of usable height (viewport minus the 40px top bar and the 44px
+ * bottom nav). Because it is sticky it never scrolls away, so the selected
+ * section rendered forever in the 94px strip below it — a heading, a divider,
+ * and no room to edit anything.
+ *
+ * The proximate cause is the breakpoint bug this family keeps hitting: the
+ * only small-screen treatment for `.section-nav` in App.css is gated on
+ * `@media (max-width: 768px)`, and a phone in landscape is *wider* than 768px
+ * (iPhone 13 -> 844, Pixel 7 -> 915). The chip-row treatment switched itself
+ * off exactly where it was needed most. Same class as #5051/#5053/#5054/#5060;
+ * see the banner in `src/components/Sidebar.css`.
+ *
